quran[20]{c,v,t}:
  76,6,(Camphor is) a spring (in Paradise) from which the servants of Allah will drink; they will make it to gush out abundantly (and flow like streams wherever they desire).
  76,7,"They fulfil their vows and fear a Day whose horror will be widespread,"
  76,8,"and give food for His love (despite their need for it) to the needy, the orphan and the prisoner,"
  76,9,"(and say:) ‘We feed you only for the sake of Allah. We do not desire any reward from you, nor thanks."
  76,10,"Indeed, We fear from our Lord the Day that will make (faces) look very dark (and) ugly.’"
  76,11,So Allah has shielded them from the horror of that Day and granted them freshness and radiance (upon their faces) and happiness (in their hearts).
  76,12,He rewarded them for being patient with a Garden and (garments of) silk.
  76,13,"Reclining there upon couches, they will find in it neither (the severe heat of) the sun nor intense cold."
  76,14,"Its shades will be close over them, and its clusters (of fruit) will be made to hang low."
  76,15,And silver vessels and shining crystal goblets will be brought around them.
  76,16,"(These goblets will be made of) gleaming crystalline silver, which they will apportion in a precise measure."
  76,17,"They will be served there with a glass of (pure) drink mixed with ginger,"
  76,18,(from) a spring therein called Salsabil.
  76,19,"Immortal youths will serve around them. When you see them, you will think they were scattered pearls."
  76,20,"As you look (at Paradise), you will see bliss (in abundance) and a great kingdom (all around)."
  76,21,Upon them will be garments of fine green silk and rich brocade. And they will be adorned with bracelets of silver. Their Lord will give them to drink a most pure drink.
  76,22,"(They will be told:) ‘This is indeed your reward, and your endeavour is well appreciated.’"
  76,23,"Indeed, We have sent down the Qur’an upon you as a piecemeal revelation."
  76,24,So (continue to) be patient with your Lord’s decree and do not listen to any sinner or disbeliever from among them.
  76,25,"And (always) celebrate the Name of your Lord, morning and evening."
